#
# Not carried:
# - the oboes as a line of their own (folded into cl; their eighth at
#   48.1, doubled by the clarinets);
# - the woodwinds' trills at 47.13-16 sound as a flutter; their
#   two-note turn into 48.1 is left out (the format has no grace note);
# - trumpets 3-6 and trombones 1-3 where they move apart from the line
#   carried (48.5-9, 49.1-6; one line a part); the tuba's held notes
#   at 48.1-4 and 49.4 (it shares tb, so its Eb is struck again with
#   each trombone note at 48.1-4);
# - the triangle (48.10-13); harp 2 throughout (one harp part);
# - the high tam-tam's quarter at 51.4 tied into 51.5;
# - the clarinets in B-flat at 49.13 (the oboes and E-flat clarinet
#   are carried);
# - the organ's manuals at 48.10-11 (not readable: rests) and the
#   second half of 48.12 (organ and pedal, not read: rests);
# - the trumpets' new attack on A4 and A5 at 47.12: their chord is
#   tied from 47.11 and play ties every note the next chord sounds
#   again, where the score ties only trumpets 3-4's Eb5.
# Changed from the readers' page files: the soprano's F5 at 49.5 is not
# tied into 49.6 (its check list reads no tie); the ties across the
# page turn at 49.9-10 (bassoons, tam-tam, organ pedal and left hand,
# cellos and basses) are written.
# Doubtful (carried as read):
# - the alto soloist's note where the altos divide, 48.3-4 (the upper);
# - the bells throughout (49.7-50.4, 51.1-12): "3 tiefe Glocken von
#   unbestimmtem Klang", no clef; the staff positions are carried at
#   their treble names, and on p. 209 the heads sit among stems;
